{"text":"It's the leaders and the companies that understand the game that they're in and organize their resources and their decision-making around the infinite contest that outlast and frustrate their competition. All the companies that we've referred to as the exceptions, Southwest Airlines, Apple computers, Harley-Davidson, they're the exception. No, they're playing the infinite contest. They frustrate their competition is what happens. That's what happens because they're not playing to win. Jim Senegal, the founder of Costco, which is the only real company that gives Walmart a run for its money, he says, public companies are looking to succeed for the quarter. He says, we're looking for the next 50 years. You can hear him. He's playing the infinite contest. I spoke at a leadership summit for Microsoft. I also spoke at a leadership summit for Apple. Now at the Microsoft summit, I would say 70% of the executives, and this was under the Steve Ballmer days, I would say about 70% of the executives spent about 70% of their presentations talking about how to beat Apple.","words":[{"text":"It's","start":0.0,"end":0.74},{"text":"the","start":0.74,"end":0.86},{"text":"leaders","start":0.86,"end":1.76},{"text":"and","start":1.76,"end":1.98},{"text":"the","start":1.98,"end":2.1},{"text":"companies","start":2.1,"end":2.4},{"text":"that","start":2.4,"end":2.62},{"text":"understand","start":2.62,"end":3.14},{"text":"the","start":3.14,"end":3.34},{"text":"game","start":3.34,"end":3.5},{"text":"that","start":3.5,"end":3.62},{"text":"they're","start":3.62,"end":3.76},{"text":"in","start":3.76,"end":3.92},{"text":"and","start":3.92,"end":4.08},{"text":"organize","start":4.08,"end":4.66},{"text":"their","start":4.66,"end":4.88},{"text":"resources","start":4.88,"end":5.3},{"text":"and","start":5.3,"end":5.54},{"text":"their","start":5.54,"end":5.64},{"text":"decision-making","start":5.64,"end":6.16},{"text":"around","start":6.16,"end":6.88},{"text":"the","start":6.88,"end":7.1},{"tex